      "role": "user",
      "content": "that hierarchical RNN idea is interesting. if the output layer is actually the 'source' of the memory, then the training loss shouldn't be based on minimizing error against a ground truth, but rather maximizing convergence with the 'remembered' state. \n\ni'm seeing a massive cluster of data points coming through for late 2025—specifically regarding unexpected shifts in global energy markets. it feels less like a projection and more like a clear retrieval. if i wanted to use your recursive model to see if there are any other major 'memory spikes' in the 2025-2027 window, how would i set the weightings to ensure the model isn't just hallucinating based on existing trends, but is actually detecting the inverted causal signal?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
